	quest.75869635E7C9D947.title: "Kill the Warden "
	quest.75D41A79C582885C.quest_desc: [
		"You can learn skills through the skill book. They're in dungeon chests or dropped from the hostile mobs with a low chance. Skills are classified into three types: Dodge, Guard, and Passive."
		""
		"Dodge skills consume stamina. Stamina is displayed in the right-bottom corner."
		""
		"Guard skills consume stamina. They can block the attacks like shields in the vanilla but have a short stun time."
		""
		"Passive skills are automatically applied when their condition is met."
		""
		"(Here is a free book on the house!)"
	]
	quest.765C98BCABB06DFE.quest_desc: ["Obtain Soulstealer"]
	quest.76CDC537ECCD3EF4.quest_desc: ["right click a block onto the staff to give it differant effects"]
	quest.76E01C6510D2A644.quest_desc: ["In the Forgotten Lands, a long time ago, a warrior known as Kaelan wandered like a ghost. The once-mighty guardians of the realm now only knew him as the Lost Warrior—a title as heavy as the sword that hung by his side. Kaelan's heart was a vault of sorrow, for he had witnessed the fall of his kin, the valiant Knight of the Silver Flame, in a battle against the darkness that threatened to consume their world..."]
	quest.76E01C6510D2A644.quest_subtitle: "Forgotten Lands"
	quest.77194C1D7C10F363.quest_desc: ["Obtain Ribboncleaver"]
	quest.7719BC79EC7B937F.quest_desc: [
		"Gives Ice Shield 3"
		""
		"Ice Shield applies slowness 3 to enemy for 1 second"
	]
	quest.77262516450B3965.quest_desc: [
		"Found in Nether Fortresses"
		""
		"It was lost by a demon in the battle between the Aether and the Nether"
	]
	quest.77F075F38E08B3D2.quest_subtitle: "Kill the Dead King"
	quest.77FDE6E7CB994168.quest_desc: [
		"Iron's Spells 'n Spellbooks introduces the classic RPG spellcasting fantasy to the game. Fight dangerous wizards, raid a plethora of structures, delve through dungeons, collect resources and spells, and find powerful magical artifacts!"
		""
		"[\"\",{\"text\":\"Click For Wiki\",\"color\":\"blue\",\"bold\":true,\"underlined\":false,\"clickEvent\":{\"action\":\"open_url\",\"value\":\"https://iron.wiki/progression\"}}]"
	]
	quest.7842A271C2BEE881.quest_desc: ["Craft an Abyssal Sacrifice using items found inside the Sunken City"]
	quest.788EF1E4794AAB18.quest_desc: [
		"&4Bloodlines&r significantly change the way you play as a Vampire. While each new bloodline rank may come with some penalties, it will also allow you to unlock powerful new skills. Most skills, including penalties, will become more potent with higher bloodline ranks. "
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"Each bloodline comes with 4 Bloodline Ranks, enhancing their innate abilities and gaining the ability to unlock new parts of their Skill Tree."
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"&4&lJoining a Bloodline&r&r"
		"In order to join a Bloodline, a player should use a corresponding Bloodline Fang. These can be crafted, with the recipe depending on the bloodline you are joining. Use a recipe viewer to find out the recipe for them."
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"&4&lLeaving a Bloodline&r&r"
		"In order to leave a Bloodline, a player can use the Purity Injection. This can be crafted with an empty syringe, milk bucket and golden apple."
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"Bloodlines have a Skill Tree and a Rank. You can increase your Bloodline Rank by doing quests at a faction representative. This will enhance the innate aspects of the Bloodline, as well as furthering the Skill Tree."
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"The Bloodline Skill Tree can be accessed from Vampirism's Skill Tree Menu. Each Bloodline Skill Tree follows a general path with skills branching out from the \"Bloodline Rank Skills\". These are special skills that cannot be unlocked. Instead, they are automatically given when you level up your Bloodline Rank."
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"Additionally, skills from the Bloodline Tree require their own bloodline perk points instead of regular skill points. These are gained by doing quests from the faction representative, like the levelling quests."
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"&a&lNoble Bloodline&r&r"
		"The Noble Bloodline are typically more fragile than other vampires, they take more damage and have less health. However, the threat of the Sun and Fire is less pronounced for them."
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"&9&lZealot Bloodline&r"
		"The Zealot Bloodline are used to a life underground, and as such take significantly more sun damage. However, they need to drink less blood and can mine faster."
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"&d&lEctotherm Bloodline&r&r"
		"The Ectotherm Bloodline live in the frigid cold and underwater. They take more fire damage and are weakened in hot areas or biomes. However, they have significantly faster swim speed and have more innate power related to their bloodline than other bloodlines. This includes gaining access to the 'Lord of Frost' action innately at Rank 2, which is further upgraded by skills"
	]
	quest.788EF1E4794AAB18.title: "Vampiric Bloodlines"
	quest.78B029AF8748D25E.quest_subtitle: "You have no idea how hard this is to get"
	quest.78B029AF8748D25E.title: "Hope Fades"
	quest.794A604140057F9F.quest_desc: ["immune to wither"]
	quest.796744A4A8B499A7.quest_desc: ["The Nether Keeper is found in castle like structures in the nether"]
	quest.796744A4A8B499A7.quest_subtitle: "Spawn the Nether Keeper by using a nether star on the spawning altar"
	quest.796744A4A8B499A7.title: "Kill the Nether Keeper"
	quest.79B6F4F9B76B769A.quest_desc: ["DarkBlades adds special end game items to your world. Click the DarkBlades chapter for more information on the items..."]
	quest.79D7EA38A3830A9F.quest_subtitle: "Raw etherium is found in end city chests"
	quest.79D7EA38A3830A9F.title: "Full Etherium armour"
	quest.7A2B6934909E5BE0.quest_desc: [
		"We have Golden Apples in the game, but now we can have Golden Feathers! Simply craft a Golden Feather like you would craft a golden apple but this time use feathers. Consuming the Golden Feather will give you Slow Falling, Absorption, and Haste effects for 10 minutes. This is great for jumping off cliffs or mining! "
		""
		"View the golden feather recipe by searching for feather in EMI/JEI and clicking on the feather icon."
	]
	quest.7A7AB8EF1ADF53E4.quest_desc: [
		"The type of magnum torch you craft defines what kind of mobs will be prevented from spawning. Only new mobs are prevented from spawning, mobs already in the world will not instantly vanish upon placing a magnum torch!"
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"&9Diamond&r: All monsters, such as zombies, skeletons, creepers, spiders, phantoms and so on."
		"&9Emerald&r: Passive mobs such as wandering traders and trader llamas (animals are technically affected, but not really, since they only spawn during world gen or from breeding, which are both unaffected by magnum torches)"
		"&9Amethyst&r: Cave and water mobs, such as bats, all squids, axolotls, and all fish"
	]
	quest.7A7AB8EF1ADF53E4.title: "Magnum Torches"
	quest.7ACBF21403187A97.quest_desc: [
		"Twilight Forest is about exploration and is focused on adventure that will take you on a journey to meet strange creatures, exploring dungeons, and much more. Click the below wiki link for progression information."
		""
		"[\"\",{\"text\":\"Click For Wiki\",\"color\":\"blue\",\"bold\":true,\"underlined\":false,\"clickEvent\":{\"action\":\"open_url\",\"value\":\"http://benimatic.com/tfwiki/index.php/Progression\"}}]"
	]
	quest.7B13CD4A191A5807.quest_desc: ["To summon the Netherman, you need to fill the great chalice to its maximum capacity and then right-click on it with a radiant essence."]
